  "body": "Found while gating #339 slice 2 (PR #492): the fixture box laws judged an arc by its **inscribed** chords at the bare band radius, so steel within the arc's sagitta (about 0.01 mm on R30) was missed. This applied to every fixture.\n\n## What changed\nNew `crates/sim/src/verify/arc_bulge.rs` (`Bulge`, `ARC_PAD` = 1e-3).\n\n**The pad.** For each chord, with ψ = |θ|/2 and θ = sweep/n (the same equal steps `arc_chords` cuts):\n- **Across the chord:** r(1 − cos ψ), the sagitta.\n- **Along the chord:** r(ψ − sin ψ).\n\nThese bound the true point against the chord point at the same sweep fraction for ψ ≤ π/2. Past a half turn, 2r is used for both. Every arc chord adds `ARC_PAD`, because arc centres sit on the 1 µm lattice.\n\n**XY arcs (box laws, `stack_span`):** the band radius grows by `hypot(across, along) + ARC_PAD`. A helix's z between joints is already exact.\n\n**XZ/YZ arcs:**\n- The radius grows by `along·|t_h| + across·|n_h| + ARC_PAD`.\n- The z window is the arc's true range between joints. Builder-split arcs are Z-monotone, so the strict-dip silence for a lead arc landing tangent on a face is kept.\n- An arc that turns past its circle's top or bottom inside a chord gets that piece's window carried to the extremum ± ARC_PAD.\n\n**Posed sweep (`posed_steel`):** an arc move's capsules grow by `Bulge::deviation()`. The interval travel already covered all but about 1e-4 mm; the pad makes the bound hold for any interval length.\n\n**Straight moves get a pad of exactly 0.0,** so every straight verdict is bit-identical.\n\n**Bad arcs fail closed:** a non-finite centre or radius gives a NaN pad, which the predicates read as a hit.\n\n`docs/decisions/491-arc-sagitta.md`\n\n## How tested\nNew sim `fixture_arc_sagitta` (10 tests). These four fail on main and pass now:\n- **The issue's repro:** R30 arc, r3 flute, 3 chords, sagitta 0.00937, box half a sagitta inside the true reach → Flute. The same arc as a rapid → Rapid.\n- The holder band is padded too.\n- An XZ arc bulging sideways reports.\n- An unsplit XZ arc dipping past its chords reports.\n\nThese also pass, as pins:\n- Steel 0.002 mm beyond the true reach stays clean.\n- A YZ arc bulging sideways reports.\n- An XZ arc landing tangent on a face stays silent, while 0.001 deeper hits.\n- A posed arc within its sagitta reports.\n- Straight moves keep their verdicts.\n- The apex sits mid-chord.\n\n**Gates:**\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick upstream/main` (all sim suites) is green.\n- The full camcraft-app suite, all 170 binaries, is green with **no existing verdict changed**. After the final syntax-only edit, sim in full and the app fixture, rotary, carried, posed-contact, arc-entry and posting suites were re-run, all green.\n- `clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --tests -D warnings` is clean.\n\n**Note:** #476's `mesh_steel` has its own `ARC_PAD` and can read `Bulge::deviation` once both land. #413 is the same family in the field engine and envelope scan, and stays its own issue.\n\nChangelog: Fixture collision laws pad each arc chord by its sagitta, so steel within an arc's bulge is no longer missed (#491)\n\nFixes #491\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
